items/fs-the-closure-of-a-path-connected-set-is-path-connected.md:58:[L1] $G$ is path-connected ([[lem-the-oscillating-zigzag-curve]], claim 1).
items/fs-the-closure-of-a-path-connected-set-is-path-connected.md:60:[L2] $\overline{G}$ is **not** path-connected ([[lem-the-oscillating-zigzag-curve]], claim 4).
items/fs-the-closure-of-a-path-connected-set-is-path-connected.md:78:- **The added set is as small as it can usefully be.** By claim 2 of [[lem-the-oscillating-zigzag-curve]], $\overline{G} \setminus G$ is one segment. So a path-connected set can lose path-connectedness on adjoining a single closed segment, and no larger or more complicated addition is needed.
