items/rem-darboux-lhopital-taylor-scope.md:24:Higher derivatives are the recursive objects of [[def-higher-derivatives-and-smoothness]]. Darboux's theorem ([[thm-darboux-theorem-for-derivatives]]) concerns every first derivative, without assuming that derivative continuous. The two L'Hôpital theorems, [[thm-lhopital-zero-over-zero]] and [[thm-lhopital-infinity-over-infinity]], require their stated derivative and nonvanishing hypotheses and do not assert converses.
