items/thm-closure-of-a-connected-set.md:83:- **Where this is used.** It is the second half of the standard method for building a connected set that is not path-connected: take a path-connected set, which is connected, and close it up. The closure is connected by this theorem regardless of how badly the added points behave, and that is what [[lem-the-oscillating-zigzag-curve]] exploits.
